Subject: [PATCH] wifi: iwlwifi: mld: map injected legacy rates to driver indices

Backport of benthecarman's proposed upstream fix:
https://lkml.iu.edu/2610.1/04784.html

mac80211 supplies an index into the current band's bitrate table. The
firmware conversion expects Intel's table, which includes four CCK rates
before OFDM. On 5 GHz the uncorrected 12 Mbps index selects 5.5 Mbps CCK,
and BE211 firmware 107.1b444747.0 asserts on the first AWDL action frame.

Keep negative indices as sentinels for the existing lowest-rate fallback.
This changes no channel permissions, power limits or regulatory handling.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/mld/tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/mld/tx.c
@@ -471,7 +471,16 @@
 		if (u32_get_bits(info->flags, IEEE80211_TX_CTL_STBC))
 			result |= RATE_MCS_STBC_MSK;
 	} else {
-		result = iwl_mld_mac80211_rate_idx_to_fw(mld, info, rate->idx);
+		int rate_idx = rate->idx;
+
+		/*
+		 * mac80211 indexes the band's bitrates, which start at
+		 * 6 Mbps outside 2.4 GHz; remap to our rate indices.
+		 */
+		if (rate_idx >= 0 && info->band != NL80211_BAND_2GHZ)
+			rate_idx += IWL_FIRST_OFDM_RATE;
+
+		result = iwl_mld_mac80211_rate_idx_to_fw(mld, info, rate_idx);
 	}
 
 	if (info->control.antennas)
